Context: this is part of the 'variations sur l'équation des lacets', a sequel to La Longue Marche (1981). It studies the action of Gal(Q̄/Q), and of Teichmüller/GT-type automorphism groups M ⊃ M^! ⊃ M^!_0, on a profinite fundamental group Π. The page works with the normaliser of an inertia (loop) generator ρ. N*_ρ is the group of automorphisms sending ρ to a conjugate of ρ^{±1}. N*_ρ/{±1} is its quotient by the sign character. The group γ_{ρ,σ} = Z^!_{ρ,σ}/L^π_0 is identified with a (quotient of the) Galois group Π_Q^~; the next page underbraces it as Π_Q^{ab}.

On page 613 Grothendieck returns to diagram (130), the homomorphism γ_{ρ,σ} → N*_ρ/{±1}. He claims it does not lift to a homomorphism into N*_ρ. Equivalently, the pull-back extension γ̃_{ρ,σ} of γ_{ρ,σ} by μ = {±1} is non-trivial.

To identify this extension he builds diagram (144):
- top row: M^![0] = Z^!_{ρ,σ} → γ_{ρ,σ} = Z^!_{ρ,σ}/L^π_0 → N*_ρ/{±1};
- vertical maps: S_0^πΓ^!_{ρ,σ} ⊂ S_0Γ^!_{ρ,σ} → M^![0], via (u,a,b) ↦ u;
- a diagonal map from S_0Γ_{ρ,σ} (without !) to γ_{ρ,σ};
- a bottom map S_0^πΓ^!_{ρ,σ} → N*_ρ.

From this he deduces a ladder of cartesian squares I, II, III, labelled (155), probably (145). Its top row is M(0) ↪ M^![0] ↠ γ_{ρ,σ} ↪ N*_ρ/{±1}. Its bottom row consists of the corresponding double covers (index 2): M(0)^~, S_0^πΓ^!, γ̃_{ρ,σ}, N*_ρ.

Here M(0)^~ is the extension of M(0) by μ induced by the extension S_0^πΓ^! of M^![0]. The next page concludes as follows. Via the canonical isomorphism M(0) ≅ γ_{ρ,σ}, the extension γ̃_{ρ,σ} is identified with M(0)^~. That extension was shown earlier to be non-trivial, so the homomorphism does not lift.

Purpose: to understand the sign ambiguity (ρ ↦ ρ^{±1}, i.e. the role of complex-conjugation-type elements τ with τ(ρ) = σ(ρ^{-1})) in the Galois/GT action on normalisers of inertia. In particular it shows that the sign cannot be split off globally.
